{"name":"Becquerel","hex":"#4bec13","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Becquerel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Becquerel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Becquerel","blocks":[{"text":"The becquerel is the unit of radioactivity in the International System of Units (SI). One becquerel is defined as an activity of one per second, on average, for aperiodic activity events referred to a radionuclide. For applications relating to human health this is a small quantity, and SI multiples of the unit are commonly used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Radium_226_radiation_source_1.jpg/330px-Radium_226_radiation_source_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Becquerel","wikidata":"Q102573"},{"title":"Becquerel (Martian crater)","blocks":[{"text":"Becquerel is a 167 km-diameter crater at 22.1°N, 352.0°E on Mars, in Arabia Terra in Oxia Palus quadrangle. It is named after Antoine H. Becquerel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Becquerel_crater_829A35_829A37.jpg/330px-Becquerel_crater_829A35_829A37.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Becquerel_(Martian_crater)","wikidata":"Q942624"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Radioactivity_and_radiation.png/500px-Radioactivity_and_radiation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Radioactivity_and_radiation.png/500px-Radioactivity_and_radiation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Graphic showing relationships between radioactivity and detected ionizing radiation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARadioactivity_and_radi